{"name":"Sunflower","hex":"#ffc512","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sunflower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The ship of characters Sunny and Basil from the videogame Omori."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sunflower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunflower (The Beach Boys album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sunflower is the sixteenth studio album by American rock band the Beach Boys. It was released by Reprise Records on August 31, 1970, and received favorable reviews but sold poorly, reaching number 151 on the US record charts during a four-week stay and becoming the lowest-charting Beach Boys album to that point. \"Add Some Music to Your Day\" was the only single from the album to chart in the US, peaking at number 64. In the UK, the album peaked at number 29."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0a/SunflowerCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunflower_(The_Beach_Boys_album)","wikidata":"Q940780"},{"title":"Sunflower (Post Malone and Swae Lee song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sunflower\" is a song by American musicians Post Malone and Swae Lee. It was released on October 18, 2018, as a single from the soundtrack to the 2018 animated film Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse, and was later included on Post Malone's third studio album Hollywood's Bleeding (2019). An official remix features fellow American singers Nicky Jam and Prince Royce."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d0/Sunflower_promo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunflower_(Post_Malone_and_Swae_Lee_song)","wikidata":"Q57939337"},{"title":"Common sunflower","blocks":[{"text":"The common sunflower is a large annual forb in the daisy family Asteraceae. The domesticated form of common sunflower is harvested for its edible seeds, which come in two types: oil and confectionery seeds. Oilseed sunflowers are widely grown globally and represent the fourth most used vegetable oil in the world. They also are used widely as bird food or as food for livestock. In contrast, confectionery sunflower seeds are often eaten as a snack food or in baking. There also are horticultural sunflower varieties that are used as plantings in domestic gardens for aesthetics. Wild plants are known for their multiple flower heads, whereas the domestic sunflower often possesses a single large flower head atop an unbranched stem."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Sunflower_sky_backdrop.jpg/330px-Sunflower_sky_backdrop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_sunflower","wikidata":"Q171497"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Dennis_Wilson_1968.jpg/250px-Dennis_Wilson_1968.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Dennis_Wilson_1968.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Dennis_Wilson_1968.jpg/250px-Dennis_Wilson_1968.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dennis Wilson begins Sunflower with his co-written song \"Slip On Through\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADennis_Wilson_1968.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/25/Bruce_Johnston_1971.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/25/Bruce_Johnston_1971.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Bruce Johnston contributed the songs \"Deirdre\" and \"Tears in the Morning\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A